00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:47.760
science? Now, I will answer this

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:51.519
question. Um so a lot of people have you

00:12:51.519 --> 00:12:53.839
have done research in like a university

00:12:53.839 --> 00:12:55.680
setting and you might have realized that

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:57.519
when you do research in a university

00:12:57.519 --> 00:13:00.160
setting um it&#x27;s sort of very insular

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:02.320
right so that only happens to people

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:03.760
like the only things that people talk

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:06.480
about are the things that like academ

00:13:06.480 --> 00:13:09.600
academics care about and so it and it

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:12.000
takes a long long time for research to

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.800
escape that and um it&#x27;s controlled by a

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:16.639
select few and like the funding is only

00:13:16.639 --> 00:13:19.120
done by people who are in government. So

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:21.120
decentralized science tries to say like

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:23.920
wouldn&#x27;t it be interesting if instead of

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:25.920
um you know science being funded by the

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:27.519
government and science being done by

00:13:27.519 --> 00:13:29.920
just in a select few number of people

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:32.240
what if instead like you democratized it

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:34.160
and sort of made like a Wikipedia or

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:36.480
like a Bitcoin equivalent for a

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:39.000
university or a re or a scientific

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:41.440
research. So that&#x27;s what um

00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:43.360
decentralized science is about. Now

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:45.760
that&#x27;s like the goal and you might have

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:47.680
questions like like what are some

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:51.200
specific things that make decentralized

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:54.279
research different from uh traditional

00:13:54.279 --> 00:13:57.440
research. Um one is the way science is

00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:00.240
validated. So uh the typical way that

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:02.320
science is done is it goes through

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.720
something called like peer review. So

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:07.279
you submit your paper to Nature or some

00:14:07.279 --> 00:14:09.680
journal and you have three um readers

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:11.839
who read over the paper and sort of rate

00:14:11.839 --> 00:14:14.000
it on a scale of 0 to five of if it

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:15.680
should be accepted and then it&#x27;s like

00:14:15.680 --> 00:14:18.000
accepted or rejected based on that. Now

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:19.760
the problem with that is like the the

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:21.760
reader or the reviewer has absolutely no

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:24.480
incentive um to do a great job at

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:25.920
validating the research because they

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:28.160
don&#x27;t make or lose any credibility or

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:30.000
money uh if they&#x27;re correct or if

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.920
they&#x27;re incorrect. So one of the things

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:34.639
that happens in decentralized science is

00:14:34.639 --> 00:14:38.320
that um you have um you have uh you have

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:42.800
people um you have people who uh want to

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:45.600
uh bet on scientific research. So

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:47.600
instead of just saying like let&#x27;s give

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:50.320
you an example let&#x27;s look at how how

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:51.920
many people here have used Polymarket.

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:53.680
So Polymarket is like what people were

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:55.600
using in the election right? So instead

00:14:55.600 --> 00:14:58.000
of going to CNN or Fox News, depending

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:00.320
on your political beliefs, um you go to

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:02.000
Polymarket. And what made Polymarket

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:05.760
really cool is that um like if if the

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:07.920
people if you were correct in in val in

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:09.440
thinking about who&#x27;s going to win the

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:11.440
election, you actually could earn money.

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:13.279
And that&#x27;s like really neat. So we want

00:15:13.279 --> 00:15:16.240
to use the same ideas in in science. So

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:18.320
if if you think a hypothesis is going to

