he&#x27;s trying to correlate these against

00:35:14.720 --> 00:35:17.440
his healthcare uh outcomes and so I

00:35:17.440 --> 00:35:18.839
thought that was very

00:35:18.839 --> 00:35:20.720
fascinating. Then there&#x27;s this guy

00:35:20.720 --> 00:35:23.280
called Quint uh who actually invented

00:35:23.280 --> 00:35:25.760
the body mass index um and then Ancel

00:35:25.760 --> 00:35:27.599
Keys renamed it to its current name of

00:35:27.599 --> 00:35:30.240
of of BMI uh in the 70s and this is

00:35:30.240 --> 00:35:32.000
another example of an early biomarker

00:35:32.000 --> 00:35:35.119
that was made finally in 1969. This is

00:35:35.119 --> 00:35:37.520
one of the seminal papers or first uh uh

00:35:37.520 --> 00:35:39.680
uh uh times that somebody wanted to make

00:35:39.680 --> 00:35:42.560
a measure of how fast a human would age.

00:35:42.560 --> 00:35:44.000
And they picked up on many different

00:35:44.000 --> 00:35:45.839
metrics. Some of them we know very well

00:35:45.839 --> 00:35:47.520
today like hand grip strength which we

00:35:47.520 --> 00:35:49.520
continue to use. Um blood pressures

