these new days, you can run an LLM. You

00:38:34.000 --> 00:38:35.520
can do deep learning on it. And you&#x27;re

00:38:35.520 --> 00:38:37.680
kind of fitting a model um to figure out

00:38:37.680 --> 00:38:39.520
how you can predict age from a blood

00:38:39.520 --> 00:38:41.680
test and from biomarkers. You then go

00:38:41.680 --> 00:38:44.000
ahead and you plot chronological age.

00:38:44.000 --> 00:38:45.920
The age that shows on your passport or

00:38:45.920 --> 00:38:47.640
your driver&#x27;s license against a

00:38:47.640 --> 00:38:51.280
biomarker predicted age. Then the next

00:38:51.280 --> 00:38:52.800
thing and this is the key step is that

00:38:52.800 --> 00:38:55.520
we create a biomarker age gap. And I

00:38:55.520 --> 00:38:56.800
want to really hammer this home because

00:38:56.800 --> 00:38:57.839
the rest of the talk is really

00:38:57.839 --> 00:38:59.040
predicated on this and it&#x27;s a

00:38:59.040 --> 00:39:00.480
fundamental concept in longevity

00:39:00.480 --> 00:39:03.040
science. We calculate a delta between

00:39:03.040 --> 00:39:05.599
the chronological age and the biomarker

00:39:05.599 --> 00:39:08.079
age. And so it turns out that if you

00:39:08.079 --> 00:39:10.240
have a positive biomarker age gap,

00:39:10.240 --> 00:39:11.359
you&#x27;re going to be predicted to be

00:39:11.359 --> 00:39:13.839
younger um than you actually are. And if

00:39:13.839 --> 00:39:15.599
you have this negative biomarker age

00:39:15.599 --> 00:39:17.760
gap, you might be predicted to be older

00:39:17.760 --> 00:39:19.520
than you actually are. And when a

00:39:19.520 --> 00:39:21.280
relative or somebody you know is telling

00:39:21.280 --> 00:39:22.720
you, oh, I&#x27;m actually, you know, my

00:39:22.720 --> 00:39:24.640
blood is younger than my actual age and

00:39:24.640 --> 00:39:25.839
they&#x27;ve done a blood test from an

00:39:25.839 --> 00:39:27.119
insurance company or something like

00:39:27.119 --> 00:39:28.880
that, this is what they&#x27;re referencing,

00:39:28.880 --> 00:39:31.839
more or less. So let&#x27;s go into our first

00:39:31.839 --> 00:39:33.680
academic paper. So this is a really

00:39:33.680 --> 00:39:35.200
wonderful nature medicine paper that

00:39:35.200 --> 00:39:37.680
came out uh two years ago now. And in

00:39:37.680 --> 00:39:40.079
this one they uh they profiled the blood

00:39:40.079 --> 00:39:42.560
of tons of patients in the UK bio bank

00:39:42.560 --> 00:39:44.800
data set um thousands of patients and

00:39:44.800 --> 00:39:47.040
they had an ensemble of uh proteins that

00:39:47.040 --> 00:39:48.960
they did feature selection on and they

00:39:48.960 --> 00:39:51.760
fit a machine learning or AI model on to

00:39:51.760 --> 00:39:54.240
predict age using proteins. In this

00:39:54.240 --> 00:39:56.320
their biomarker is called protein age

00:39:56.320 --> 00:39:58.240
pro age and their biomarker age gap is

00:39:58.240 --> 00:40:00.640
called the protein age gap. The plot on

00:40:00.640 --> 00:40:03.040
the left is the UK bio bank showing

00:40:03.040 --> 00:40:05.359
their protein age plotted against um age

00:40:05.359 --> 00:40:07.599
in the in the cohort. Um and they show a

00:40:07.599 --> 00:40:10.000
very tight fit. The piercing correlation

00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:12.560
is 0.94. And this is their test set. But

00:40:12.560 --> 00:40:14.079
the thing that&#x27;s remarkable is that

00:40:14.079 --> 00:40:15.760
although this was trained in the UK,

00:40:15.760 --> 00:40:17.920
they profiled the blood of a Chinese

00:40:17.920 --> 00:40:19.839
data set and they got an extremely tight

00:40:19.839 --> 00:40:22.400
fit in a a kind of a blinded test set

00:40:22.400 --> 00:40:24.000
and a piercing correlation coefficient

00:40:24.000 --> 00:40:27.000
as well of 0.92. And so even

00:40:27.000 --> 00:40:29.119
geographically, culturally, you know,

00:40:29.119 --> 00:40:31.520
genetic or or e ethnically different

00:40:31.520 --> 00:40:33.280
groups, they actually were able to fit

00:40:33.280 --> 00:40:35.839
age uh in kind of a blinded unbiased way

00:40:35.839 --> 00:40:38.240
in a training and test cohort. And so

00:40:38.240 --> 00:40:39.440
what&#x27;s the big deal? What can you do

00:40:39.440 --> 00:40:41.359
with this protein age? Well, it turns

00:40:41.359 --> 00:40:43.200
out that if you kind of have a very

